WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:07.395
Bobby entered the kitchen and smiled at his friends.

2
00:00:07.396 --> 00:00:10.595
"Cooking class will be great today!"

3
00:00:10.596 --> 00:00:13.472
"Why?" Izzie asked.

4
00:00:13.473 --> 00:00:19.565
"Bobby, should we tell the others about your guest?" Chef smiled.

5
00:00:19.566 --> 00:00:24.811
"Not yet," Bobby said. "Let's surprise them."

6
00:00:24.812 --> 00:00:30.141
"Sounds good." Chef nodded and pointed to the recipe screen.

7
00:00:30.142 --> 00:00:33.055
"We're making oatmeal raisin cookies today.

8
00:00:33.056 --> 00:00:36.690
They'll be dessert for the sack lunches we'll pack.

9
00:00:36.691 --> 00:00:40.516
Bobby will tell you more about the lunches later."

10
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:44.441
"Why the big secret?" Jason asked.

11
00:00:44.442 --> 00:00:47.941
Bobby just grinned.

12
00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:53.064
Chef heated the oven to 175 degrees Celsius.

13
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:56.195
"Let's mix the dry ingredients."

14
00:00:56.196 --> 00:01:00.258
Bobby measured the flour and poured it into a bowl.

15
00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:04.412
Nina added one teaspoon of baking soda.

16
00:01:04.413 --> 00:01:08.170
Izzie put in one teaspoon of cinnamon.

17
00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:12.029
Jason poured in a half teaspoon of salt.

18
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.097
Bobby mixed the ingredients together.

19
00:01:15.098 --> 00:01:19.895
Next, Izzie measured three-quarters of a cup of brown sugar.

20
00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:23.257
She got a spoon and packed it down.

21
00:01:23.258 --> 00:01:26.473
"Pack it firmly," Bobby said.

22
00:01:26.474 --> 00:01:31.087
Izzie rolled her eyes. "I am!"

23
00:01:31.088 --> 00:01:35.233
She dumped the brown sugar into another mixing bowl.

24
00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:38.910
Nina poured in half a cup of white sugar.

25
00:01:38.911 --> 00:01:42.684
Jason added 14 tablespoons of butter.

26
00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:46.063
"That's a lot of butter," Bobby said.

27
00:01:46.064 --> 00:01:48.537
"But I can do the mixing!

28
00:01:48.538 --> 00:01:51.511
I know how to get out all the lumps."

29
00:01:51.512 --> 00:01:55.874
He mixed the butter and sugars until the mixture looked creamy.

30
00:01:55.875 --> 00:01:59.450
Izzie added vanilla.

31
00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:02.841
Nina cracked two eggs.

32
00:02:02.842 --> 00:02:07.472
"Don't get any shells in there," Bobby snapped.

33
00:02:07.473 --> 00:02:10.950
"I won't!" Nina said.

34
00:02:10.951 --> 00:02:14.955
"Bobby! Stop being so bossy," Jason said.

35
00:02:14.956 --> 00:02:18.797
"I want these cookies to be perfect."

36
00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:22.300
Bobby mixed the ingredients again.

37
00:02:22.301 --> 00:02:26.580
"Now add the dry ingredients," Chef said.

38
00:02:26.581 --> 00:02:29.905
"I'll do it!" Bobby said.

39
00:02:29.906 --> 00:02:34.447
"It's Izzie's turn to use the mixer," Chef said.

40
00:02:34.448 --> 00:02:37.575
Bobby frowned, but he stepped aside.

41
00:02:37.576 --> 00:02:41.563
Izzie added the dry ingredients to the butter mixture.

42
00:02:41.564 --> 00:02:45.666
Then she started mixing.

43
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:51.218
Jason poured in three cups of oats while Nina added raisins.

44
00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:54.066
Izzie mixed the dough again.

45
00:02:54.067 --> 00:03:00.019
Everyone took turns dropping spoonfuls of dough onto a baking sheet.

46
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:04.960
"Nina, yours are too close together," Bobby said.

47
00:03:04.961 --> 00:03:08.468
"And Jason's are too small."

48
00:03:08.469 --> 00:03:16.024
Chef sighed. "They're doing fine, Bobby."

49
00:03:16.025 --> 00:03:19.024
Nina put the sheet in the oven.

50
00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:22.703
Chef set the timer for eight minutes.

51
00:03:22.704 --> 00:03:26.366
"Time to make the sandwiches," he said.

52
00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:29.520
The kids made tuna salad sandwiches.

53
00:03:29.521 --> 00:03:32.025
They put each one in a sack.

54
00:03:32.026 --> 00:03:35.445
They added carrot sticks and an apple.

55
00:03:35.446 --> 00:03:39.332
The timer went off.

56
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:42.412
"Let's check the cookies," Chef said.

57
00:03:42.413 --> 00:03:45.581
"They should be golden brown."

58
00:03:45.582 --> 00:03:50.420
The cookies looked perfect.

59
00:03:50.421 --> 00:03:53.572
After they had cooled, everyone ate one.

60
00:03:53.573 --> 00:03:57.891
"They're great!" Bobby said, grinning.

61
00:03:57.892 --> 00:04:02.253
The kids put a cookie in each sack.

62
00:04:02.254 --> 00:04:05.905
"Hi, kids!" someone said.

63
00:04:05.906 --> 00:04:09.063
"Grandpa!" Bobby shouted.

64
00:04:09.064 --> 00:04:12.129
"The lunches are ready."

65
00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.137
"Thank you for making these," Grandpa said.

66
00:04:16.138 --> 00:04:21.914
"The lunches are for older people in our neighborhood," Bobby said.

67
00:04:21.915 --> 00:04:26.668
"Grandpa says they sometimes have trouble getting out to shop for food.

68
00:04:26.669 --> 00:04:31.366
Some don't have much money, so they might skip meals.

69
00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:34.993
I asked Chef if we could help them."

70
00:04:34.994 --> 00:04:39.380
"Great idea!" Nina smiled at Grandpa.

71
00:04:39.381 --> 00:04:42.293
Izzie and Jason nodded.

72
00:04:42.294 --> 00:04:46.617
"Now Grandpa and I will deliver these," Bobby said.

73
00:04:46.618 --> 00:04:49.428
"Thanks for helping!"

